563
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:44,350
(fully settle into this environment.)
Their distance right now

564
00:16:44,350 --> 00:16:45,340
(I may need two days to adjust...)
is quite interesting too.

565
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:47,000
Look, they're sitting
on the same sofa

566
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,360
(and get more familiar with everyone.)
and chatting happily.

567
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:50,480
But there's a cushion between them.

568
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:53,720
It's that feeling of liking someone
you've just met

569
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:55,480
while deliberately

570
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,840
keeping a little distance between you.

571
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,700
You just seem so cheerful

572
00:16:59,700 --> 00:17:00,360
and outgoing.

573
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:00,960
You came in all smiles,

574
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:02,090
going, "Ah".

575
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,630
What do you mean, going, "Ah"?

576
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:05,480
That's why I said

577
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:08,280
it felt like love at first sight.

578
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:09,240
I think

579
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:11,120
her body language like this

580
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:11,960
showed

581
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:13,840
how happy she was.

582
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:15,720
Look, he moved the cushion away.

583
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,480
The one between them.

584
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:18,160
It feels like the distance

585
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:20,200
between their hearts has closed too.

586
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:21,480
These little gestures

587
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:23,080
can actually reveal

588
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:24,960
how their feelings are changing.

589
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,720
Now I finally understand

590
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,680
why people ship couples.

591
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:42,480
I think there's a signal

592
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:44,200
between Yu Yang and Liang Renfang.

593
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:45,760
Do you think attraction

594
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:47,000
can develop that quickly?

595
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:49,840
What were we like back then?

596
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,880
On our first day in the house,

597
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:53,560
I was cooking.

598
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:55,240
When Lan came in,

599
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,400
I noticed her.

600
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:57,480
Back then, I was still

601
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:58,360
really shy.

602
00:17:58,680 --> 00:17:59,600
I might show you

603
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,440
that I liked you,

604
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:02,760
but you know me.

605
00:18:02,760 --> 00:18:04,160
In front of so many people,

606
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,760
I couldn't bring myself

607
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:06,640
to stare at you again.

608
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:10,200
I think attraction can happen quickly.

609
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:14,160
We were actually a lot like them.

610
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:15,360
There was an unspoken connection

611
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:16,920
between the two of us.

612
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:18,680
Then we'd have

613
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:20,920
our own one-on-one conversations.

614
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:24,120
We'd form our own little bubble.

615
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:24,880
That does happen.

616
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,280
I forgot to tell you something.

617
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:26,760
Go ahead.

618
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:28,120
I arrived quite early that day.

619
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:30,640
I waited ages for you.

620
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,080
Really?

621
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:31,400
Yes.

622
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:33,000
But when you finally came in,

623
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,480
I wasn't as excited as I expected.

624
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:35,240
Really?

625
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:35,800
It's just...

626
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:36,520
Why?

627
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:38,600
It wasn't that I liked you any less.

628
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:39,760
It was just strange.

629
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:40,720
I'd waited so long,

630
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:41,920
but when you finally came in,

631
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:44,240
I started pretending to be calm.

632
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:47,320
But I never doubted my feelings

633
00:18:47,320 --> 00:18:49,680
or thought I liked you any less.

634
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,190
Do you want some water?

635
00:18:57,100 --> 00:18:58,580
(Signals with his eyes)

636
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:00,090
I do.

637
00:19:00,090 --> 00:19:01,820
Shall we go get some?

638
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:03,300
(Pulls her along)

639
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:05,030
Let's get some water.

640
00:19:05,330 --> 00:19:05,770
Okay.

641
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:09,480
Why did everyone leave?

642
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:11,000
Everyone knows how to read the room.

643
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:13,080
They left the first floor to those two.

644
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:17,400
What's wrong with her?

645
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:18,840
What happened?

646
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:19,960
What's going on?

647
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,680
(Be brave)

648
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:22,320
Be brave.

649
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:22,920
She's encouraging herself.

650
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:24,160
That's really

651
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:24,560
kind of cute.

652
00:19:26,390 --> 00:19:27,860
I need to make the first move.

653
00:19:27,860 --> 00:19:28,570
Take the initiative.

654
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:29,770
I have to try.

655
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:30,680
Taking the initiative

656
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:31,680
is actually quite hard.

657
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:33,680
(Pulls herself together)
Right.

658
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:34,920
Especially for an introvert.

659
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:35,590
Zhao Xilun,

660
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:37,530
do you want to go for a walk together?

661
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:39,080
She's rehearsing.

662
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:42,880
(Hello)
That's so direct.

663
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:44,900
We gave them some time alone.

664
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:45,760
Oh no.

665
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:47,640
(Looks back)
What if you don't get time alone now?

666
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:50,100
(Looks back)

667
00:19:50,100 --> 00:19:53,140
(A chance?)

668
00:19:53,140 --> 00:19:53,880
Look.

669
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:54,960
Oh no.

670
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:56,860
(Done getting water, then called away)
We're done getting water.

671
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:57,920
Oh no.

672
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:58,900
(Anxious; walks downstairs)

673
00:19:59,120 --> 00:19:59,840
What now?

674
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:03,000
(Scratches his head)
Such bad timing.

675
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:03,840
With someone else there,

676
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:05,120
it's hard to ask him.

677
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:07,180
(Gets up too)

678
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:08,370
You're reading?

679
00:20:09,710 --> 00:20:10,760
There's
"Stories about Ming Dynasty" here.

680
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,080
Four guys

681
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:13,720
(What's this? "The Red and the Black")
are all in here talking to her.

682
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:18,910
(Picks up a book)
This one suits me.

683
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:20,600
(I owe you an apology)
Look at him by the bookshelf.

684
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:21,660
What?

685
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:22,890
What's this called?

686
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:25,310
"Zero to One".

687
00:20:25,670 --> 00:20:26,770
It's about entrepreneurship.

688
00:20:27,780 --> 00:20:28,770
I've read it.

689
00:20:28,850 --> 00:20:29,880
(Joins the conversation)
I'm just taking a look.

690
00:20:30,210 --> 00:20:31,110
Do you want to start a business?

691
00:20:31,110 --> 00:20:32,560
(Changes the subject)
So, you want to visit the Ming dynasty?

692
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:33,560
That joke was a little too dry.

693
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:35,120
(Looks over)
Bro, that was a little too dry.

694
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:36,380
(The Ming dynasty is interesting, though)
He's forcing the conversation.

695
00:20:38,420 --> 00:20:39,420
(Turns and leaves)

696
00:20:41,010 --> 00:20:43,180
Does your major
involve more essay writing or...

697
00:20:43,180 --> 00:20:43,870
(Tries another topic)
Essay writing.

698
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,240
They've all left.

699
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:47,640
Everyone was waiting
for someone to leave first.

700
00:20:47,810 --> 00:20:48,630
Why did you come downstairs?

701
00:20:48,630 --> 00:20:49,910
Wasn't I just beside you?

702
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:51,060
You were beside me?

703
00:20:51,060 --> 00:20:51,680
Right.

704
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:52,920
So much keeps happening.

705
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:53,840
This is so entertaining.

706
00:20:54,570 --> 00:20:55,470
I have a friend at Imperial College too.

707
00:20:55,850 --> 00:20:56,930
You know someone from our school?

708
00:20:56,930 --> 00:20:57,600
I do.

709
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:58,440
They're in your major.

710
00:20:58,670 --> 00:20:59,910
That's why I asked you that day.

711
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:02,240
("Mr. Inbetween", An infallible assassin)
An infallible assassin?

712
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:06,280
When Sha Yue'er was in the study,

713
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:08,000
if that many people
came in to talk to her,

714
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,040
what would you do?

715
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:12,960
I'd just listen to them talk.

716
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:13,680
Lan,

717
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:14,920
how would you react

718
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:17,040
if the guy you liked

719
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:17,760
or were interested in

720
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:19,960
walked into the study?

721
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:21,080
I think

722
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:23,080
I'd make it clear
he was special to me.

723
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:25,760
I'd make eye contact with him.

724
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:28,640
I'd look at him as soon as he walked in.

725
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:29,080
Right.

726
00:21:29,840 --> 00:21:33,160
So he wouldn't feel ignored
or uncomfortable

727
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:34,840
and want to leave.

728
00:21:34,840 --> 00:21:38,080
I'd also talk to him more.

729
00:21:38,080 --> 00:21:41,320
I'd pick up on what he said
and keep the conversation going.

730
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:44,600
I wasn't trying to leave.

731
00:21:50,840 --> 00:21:51,920
That's great.

732
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:53,560
If you

733
00:21:53,560 --> 00:21:57,000
gave me that kind of positive response,

734
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:58,440
I'd probably leave

735
00:21:58,440 --> 00:21:59,240
feeling really happy.

736
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:01,640
Wouldn't you worry...

737
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:02,320
(Confident)
No.

738
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:04,520
about what the others inside
were talking about?

739
00:22:04,520 --> 00:22:05,320
There's no need to worry.

740
00:22:05,320 --> 00:22:06,440
What's yours will always be yours.

741
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:07,840
Right.

742
00:22:09,820 --> 00:22:11,040
My earring fell off.

743
00:22:14,290 --> 00:22:14,590
It's okay.

744
00:22:14,590 --> 00:22:15,730
Don't bother looking.

745
00:22:15,730 --> 00:22:16,590
We'll never find it.

746
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:19,280
That doesn't have
a hidden meaning, does it?

747
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:20,520
They'll never

748
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:21,240
find the earring.

749
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:23,760
And he lost her too.

750
00:22:24,850 --> 00:22:25,470
I'll go get some water.

751
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:26,080
She left.

752
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:27,880
Did she use that as an excuse to leave?

753
00:22:32,630 --> 00:22:33,420
I once saw a quote

754
00:22:33,420 --> 00:22:34,250
that I thought was really good.

755
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:36,300
Extremely arrogant people

756
00:22:36,300 --> 00:22:38,080
are actually deeply insecure.

757
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:40,120
Yes, deep down, I'm very arrogant.

758
00:22:40,120 --> 00:22:40,770
I often feel

759
00:22:40,770 --> 00:22:41,370
that even people I'm close to

760
00:22:41,370 --> 00:22:43,380
can be foolish in many ways.

761
00:22:43,380 --> 00:22:44,670
Yet deep down, I'm insecure.

762
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:46,390
I also feel

763
00:22:46,390 --> 00:22:47,760
that they're better than me
in many ways.

764
00:22:48,620 --> 00:22:50,090
I often compare my weaknesses

765
00:22:50,090 --> 00:22:51,560
with other people's strengths.

766
00:22:51,560 --> 00:22:53,040
I'm afraid I'm not good enough.

767
00:22:53,210 --> 00:22:54,770
I feel that if I'm not good enough,

768
00:22:54,770 --> 00:22:55,960
someone will

769
00:22:56,250 --> 00:22:57,200
leave me one day.

770
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:04,680
He's completely

771
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:05,520
opened himself up?

772
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:06,440
Yes.

773
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:07,560
They're having

774
00:23:07,560 --> 00:23:08,200
a deep conversation.

775
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:09,120
They've gone really deep.

776
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:11,900
I didn't expect to tell you this.

777
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:13,660
But suddenly, I wanted to.

778
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:15,710
It's okay. I'll...

779
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:18,840
Now they share a secret.

780
00:23:20,410 --> 00:23:21,770
From what I've learned
about you so far,

781
00:23:21,770 --> 00:23:22,820
I think you're quite impressive.

782
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:24,790
I think you're impressive too.

783
00:23:24,790 --> 00:23:26,700
That's what I was waiting to hear.

784
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:27,840
He got the validation he wanted.

785
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:28,640
Do you think it's because

786
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:30,200
they've had similar experiences,

787
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,560
so they can

788
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:33,760
relate to each other on many things?

789
00:23:37,510 --> 00:23:38,160
Hello.

790
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:39,130
Hello.

791
00:23:39,460 --> 00:23:40,340
Let's go for a walk.

792
00:23:43,840 --> 00:23:45,020
You meet

793
00:23:45,020 --> 00:23:46,180
so many people every day.

794
00:23:46,930 --> 00:23:47,790
Haven't you ever

795
00:23:47,790 --> 00:23:49,380
met your ideal type?

796
00:23:50,080 --> 00:23:50,960
She asked him directly.

797
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:52,880
I think she wants

798
00:23:52,880 --> 00:23:54,080
to know whether his ideal type

799
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:55,840
is someone like her.

800
00:23:55,900 --> 00:23:57,170
When you switched seats that day,

801
00:23:57,170 --> 00:23:58,590
did you just choose randomly?

802
00:23:59,140 --> 00:23:59,940
(Wow)

803
00:23:59,940 --> 00:24:00,900
(So direct)

804
00:24:01,280 --> 00:24:02,620
You have to respect the person you like.

805
00:24:02,620 --> 00:24:03,360
They might want to get to know...

806
00:24:03,950 --> 00:24:05,220
Get to know someone else too, right?

807
00:24:06,990 --> 00:24:08,080
I'm just giving an example.

808
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:08,880
That's what I mean.

809
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:10,760
What now?

810
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:12,960
She's also

811
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:14,080
quite direct.

812
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:15,320
But I think

813
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:16,200
although she's direct,

814
00:24:16,200 --> 00:24:17,400
she's actually very sensitive.

815
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:20,360
She asks everything
she wants to know directly

816
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:21,520
and sees how he responds.

817
00:24:21,520 --> 00:24:23,800
I think she handled it quite well.

818
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:25,160
Actually, I think Sun Bohan

819
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:25,800
was trying

820
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:27,960
to explain what was going
through his mind.

821
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:29,920
I just don't think
he explained it clearly.

822
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:31,280
Right. He was too vague.

823
00:24:31,280 --> 00:24:32,240
Far too vague.

824
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:33,560
He could've just said it directly.

825
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:35,880
What if

826
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:38,200
you two were in that situation,

827
00:24:38,600 --> 00:24:39,640
would you ask directly?

828
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:42,600
Let me put myself in her shoes.

829
00:24:42,840 --> 00:24:43,720
I wouldn't.

830
00:24:43,720 --> 00:24:44,760
Neither would I.

831
00:24:45,680 --> 00:24:47,160
I'd keep observing.

832
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:47,880
Me too.

833
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:48,720
I wouldn't dare.

834
00:24:48,720 --> 00:24:49,480
I'm too timid.

835
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,440
Are the signal lines starting to form?

836
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:58,040
Looks like it.

837
00:24:58,500 --> 00:24:59,680
(Cui Kaiyi to Cao Yiheng: Hope
to see your livelier side. Rest well.)

838
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:00,360
Wait,

839
00:25:00,360 --> 00:25:02,520
Cui Kaiyi sent her message to...

840
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:05,480
So Sun Bohan's answer just now

841
00:25:05,480 --> 00:25:07,360
actually changed

842
00:25:07,360 --> 00:25:08,160
who she wanted

843
00:25:08,160 --> 00:25:10,440
to get to know.

844
00:25:10,440 --> 00:25:11,880
I can't find my earring.

845
00:25:13,840 --> 00:25:15,400
That was a meaningful conversation.

846
00:25:15,760 --> 00:25:17,000
Right.

847
00:25:17,970 --> 00:25:19,120
(Sha Yue'er to Chen Hewen:
Get some rest.)

848
00:25:19,160 --> 00:25:20,600
